Boundary near-misses for diag.identifier_too_long: an effective name of
exactly 20 characters after stripping the s prefix (raw length 21), and a
procedure name of exactly 30 characters. A name whose character after
the would-be prefix is lowercase (notesForTheShiftHandover) is measured
whole: 24 characters, so it fires.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ArchiveCompletedWorkOrderBatch;
	:DECLARE sAbcdefghijklmnopqrst, notesForTheShiftHandover;
	sAbcdefghijklmnopqrst := "x";
	notesForTheShiftHandover := sAbcdefghijklmnopqrst;
	:RETURN notesForTheShiftHandover;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ArchiveCompletedWorkOrderBatch;
	:DECLARE sAbcdefghijklmnopqrst, notesForTheShiftHandover;

	sAbcdefghijklmnopqrst := "x";
	notesForTheShiftHandover := sAbcdefghijklmnopqrst;

	:RETURN notesForTheShiftHandover;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:34-2:58 info identifier_too_long: Variable name 'notesForTheShiftHandover' exceeds 20-character limit (effective length 24 excluding prefix)
